  "notes": "{運|うん} means luck, fortune, or fate - chance events beyond one's control.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {運|うん}がいい: lucky, fortunate\n- {運|うん}が{悪|わる}い: unlucky\n- {運|うん}を{試|ため}す: to try one's luck\n- {運|うん}に{任|まか}せる: to leave it to fate\n- {運|うん}が{向|む}く: luck turns (in one's favor)\n- {運|うん}が{尽|つ}きる: luck runs out\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n- {運命|うんめい}: fate, destiny\n- {幸運|こううん}: good fortune\n- {不運|ふうん}: misfortune, bad luck\n- {運勢|うんせい}: fortune (as in horoscope)\n\nCULTURE:\n{運|うん} plays an important role in Japanese culture, with concepts like {縁起|えんぎ} (omens) and fortune-telling ({占|うらな}い) being common.",
